  "nav_about": "About",
  "meta_about": "About · Gitscout",
  "about_title": "How Gitscout works",
  "about_score_intro": "Each of the six stats runs from 0 to 100. The overall rating is their weighted average, using the shares below.",
  "about_stat_act": "Contributions in the last year",
  "about_stat_imp": "Stars and forks on your repos",
  "about_stat_com": "Your followers",
  "about_stat_rep": "PRs merged into other people's repos, and code reviews",
  "about_stat_con": "How regularly you contribute",
  "about_stat_exp": "How many years you've been building",
  "about_story_title": "The idea",
  "about_story_1": "We turn your GitHub contributions, stars and PRs into a collectible card game: get your card, duel a friend, see where you land on the leaderboard. Scores only measure visible work; the real fun is in the comparing.",
  "about_score_note": "The first points come quickly and the top gets harder: full marks take extreme values (for example {followers} followers). Most active developers get silver or gold; 90+ is for the very best.",
  "about_privacy_body": "All data comes from GitHub's public API. Private repos are never read, and no email or other contact details are stored. Anonymous, cookie-free visit statistics help improve the site.",
  "about_lead": "Turns a public GitHub profile into a collectible card. Scores come from open formulas, not AI.",
  "about_stats_title": "How is the rating calculated?",
  "about_rarity": "{rarity}: {range}",
  "about_faq_title": "FAQ",
  "about_faq_low_q": "Why is my rating low?",
  "about_faq_low_a": "Gitscout only looks at work that's publicly visible on GitHub. Work in private repos or on other platforms isn't seen. Stats are logarithmic too, so the first points come easily and the top is hard.",
  "about_faq_refresh_q": "When does my rating change?",
  "about_faq_refresh_a": "Cards refresh automatically every {days} days. Activity looks at the last year, so your rating can move up and down. If a mistake or unfairness turns up in the formula, it's fixed and everyone's rating is recalculated.",
  "about_faq_bots_q": "Do automated commits inflate the rating?",
  "about_faq_bots_a": "No. A single day counts for at most {daily} contributions. Commits beyond {repo} a year in one repo are treated as automation and deducted.",
  "about_faq_org_q": "How are organization repos counted?",
  "about_faq_org_a": "Stars and forks go to Impact in proportion to your share of the last year's commits; at {share} or more of the commits, they count in full. PRs to an organization you maintain count at {weight} weight in Reputation.",
  "about_faq_role_q": "How are my role and badges decided?",
  "about_faq_role_a": "Your role comes from the languages in your repos: the biggest share wins, and if both Frontend and Backend are at {share} or more, you're Full Stack. Badges reward things like long streaks or lots of reviews and don't change your rating.",
  "about_privacy_title": "Data and privacy",
  "about_privacy_removal": "Anyone can add any username. If you'd rather not be on the leaderboard, open an issue and your card will be removed.",
  "about_privacy_issue": "Open an issue",
